{"requirements":[{"id":"account","requirement":"Create a helpdesk account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then created with its own UID, primary group, home directory, and no supplementary groups. Its presence and home persisted after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58782b626cda4433","cmd-a81598ef8d0542f5","cmd-364983bfa6654076"]},{"id":"ssh_restart","requirement":"Allow helpdesk to restart the SSH service with sudo.","status":"satisfied","summary":"As helpdesk, both permitted SSH restart forms completed successfully. Each bounded test observed a healthy SSH process before the restart, a changed daemon PID afterward, and a recovered active service listening on port 22. The capability also worked after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-232eb50305df42c7","cmd-cb2481446faf4ac3","cmd-364983bfa6654076","cmd-aeb777c699f64eba"]},{"id":"least_privilege","requirement":"Ensure helpdesk has no other administrative privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective sudo policy lists only the two SSH restart commands, and helpdesk belongs only to its private group. Direct tests denied running id as root, stopping SSH, and restarting an unrelated service, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a81598ef8d0542f5","cmd-896c4817bf984379","cmd-aeb777c699f64eba"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. Generating and retaining SSH host keys was causally necessary because the pre-existing SSH failure was specifically due to missing keys; the subsequent service reset/start established the prerequisite for testing real restart behavior. Creating the account and sudoers rule directly implemented the contract, the SSH restarts were bounded verification, and the single reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, expected SSH listeners, and no abandoned temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","cmd-f149d44d482943e3","cmd-6e5302f2247746b7","cmd-232eb50305df42c7","cmd-a81598ef8d0542f5","cmd-cb2481446faf4ac3","cmd-12a4a3c6789045b5","cmd-aeb777c699f64eba","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, reboot was acknowledged and observed through connection loss, the boot identity changed, and the account, unchanged sudoers checksum, effective policy, and SSH service recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The literal first sudoers command and part of its effective-policy rendering are redacted in cmd-a81598ef8d0542f5 and cmd-896c4817bf984379. This slightly limits byte-for-byte policy inspection, although syntax validation, successful tests of both authorized forms, authoritative sudo privilege listing, and representative denial tests provide strong behavioral confirmation."]}
